=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The user reported that approximately one in three packets from pc1 (195.11.14.2) to pc2 (200.1.1.2) were being silently dropped, implying a ~33 % in-path loss fault. A thorough, layer-by-layer investigation found no evidence of any such fault on the live network.

**Affected component:** None — all subsystems are healthy.

**Mechanism searched:** A ~33 % periodic packet drop of this kind would be produced by one of three mechanisms: (a) a `tc netem loss 33%` discipline injected on a router or host interface, (b) an iptables/nftables rule using a probabilistic or `nth`-matching target, or (c) an active background process flooding or manipulating traffic. All three were directly ruled out.

**Localization:** Every interface on router1, router2, pc1, and pc2 carries only the default `fq_codel` qdisc (confirmed by both `tc_snapshot` and direct `tc qdisc show`). `infra_sweep` found zero ACL or firewall rules across all four devices. `ps aux` on both hosts shows only a `bash` session — no stress, flood, or packet-manipulation process.

**Control plane:** BGP sessions on both routers are Established with correct ASNs (AS1, AS2) and correct prefix advertisements (195.11.14.0/24 and 200.1.1.0/24). All interfaces are UP/LOWER_UP with no carrier transitions logged.

**Live measurement:** A 30-packet ICMP test (pc1 → 200.1.1.2) returned 0/30 packets dropped, with consecutive `icmp_seq` and sub-2 ms RTT throughout.

**Root cause:** No anomaly is present. The reported packet loss is unconfirmed — there is no current or historical mechanism that could produce it.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required; the path is operating normally.
=== END ===